        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(1) Establishment of Welfare Benefits Trust. The parties recognize that the actual cost of the postretirement healthcare benefits to be made available to Eligible Participants through the Retiree Medical Plan and the Retiree Dental Plan exceeds the level established by the Retiree Healthcare Caps and that the excess cost would, in the absence of further funding, have to be met by premium (or other) payments by Eligible Participants. The parties further recognize that the additional costs that the Eligible Participants would have to absorb may make further participation in the retiree healthcare program prohibitive for many.",
